  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building &amp; Programme Consolidation for AHISDO and CBISDO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Many people living in the slums of Addis Ababa survive on less than $1 a day.  Housing, water, sanitation and other services are of poor quality.   Sustainable community-led programmes responding to the needs of slum dwellers are therefore needed desperately. This project will support local organisations helping communities improve housing and community infrastructure, support work that enables the poorest members of the community to gain vocational training and loans so they are able to earn a living and ensure they have access to basic health and other services.  As a result of this, more people will experience better health, and be able to earn a living.</narrative>
  </description>
